      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Optical lattice clocks are an exceptional advance in precision measurement, enabling unprecedented timekeeping and new tests of fundamental physics.",
        "attribution": "Katori and Ye are the two decisive and readily identifiable pioneers of the optical-lattice-clock approach.",
        "maturity": "Independent laboratories have demonstrated remarkable accuracy, reproducibility, and broad scientific utility over many years.",
        "uncertainties": [
